<br/>There are three item-level versions of tier gear in this phase, starting with the 251 item-level version bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a>. This tier has a layered system, requiring a previous piece and a corresponding mark to upgrade. You can potentially get the Legs and Gloves from the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4603/vault-of-archavon">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Vault of Archavon</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>You will have to <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/wotlk/warlock/" target="_blank">simulate</a> your setup to determine which upgrades and pieces make the most sense to get first as a lot of this will depend on your current equipment. Alternatively, you can also look over at the results from the <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1poD9jIP52sE7k7e30PN-5GYuGPU0nR_bPWZt599MGik/edit#gid=1351878064" target="_blank">Warlock Simulation Competition</a> to see various setups and how they fare compared to the absolute best in slot setup.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems">Gems</h4>For gemming, you will want to use these slots to balance out your Hit and reach your meta gem requirement. Most often it is not worthwhile to get the gem bonus unless it is a spell damage, hit, or haste bonus. For more in-depth info on gems, see the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warlock/destruction/dps-enchants-gems-pve">Gem Guide.</a> Destruction is a bit unique when it comes to yellow gems. There are "soft haste caps" where additional Haste will result in slightly out of sync rotation which result in lower DPS. Your gems are an ideal place to play around this, gemming <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40155/reckless-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Ametrine</span></a> until you reach the sweet spot, after which you fill the rest with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40152/potent-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Potent Ametrine</span></a>. The easiest method to determine the amount of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40155/reckless-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Ametrine</span></a> you need will be by using <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/wotlk/warlock/" target="_blank">Wowsims</a>.<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Meta Socket - <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41285/chaotic-skyflare-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_icediamond_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chaotic Skyflare Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
