<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Warlock DPS in Phase 4</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head</h3>One of the most important slots for achieving our four-piece set bonus from <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-840/dark-covens-regalia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Coven's Regalia</span></a> is the head. It makes for the biggest loss in performance if we give up on the head slot and instead opt for using a non-tier piece here. Luckily this phase we can choose in which order we get our tier pieces as we can buy them using <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> and upgrade with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52027/conquerors-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> or the heroic version. In general, it is also recommended to simulate your specific gearing upgrade path when it comes to tier 10, sometimes it will be more beneficial to upgrade to another slot first if you did not get luck on your side last phase. However, most often the tier 10 helm will be the biggest tier piece upgrade available.<br/>
<br/>It should be noted that the most valid helmets this phase up to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47796/guldans-hood-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_139.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gul'dan's Hood of Triumph</span></a> from last phase all do not have any hit rating on them, making it easy to swap in and out of helms without having to account for your hit rating changing and needing to swap in a secondary item. Note this does not account for any set bonuses.<div class="box">
<b>Head Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50368/arcanum-of-burning-mysteries">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Burning Mysteries</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44075/arcanum-of-dominance">
